## Dev backend env template ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â copy to backend/.env or backend/.env.dev.
## Missing keys fall back to code defaults (see internal/config/config.go).
## The browser-facing origin is a SINGLE switch: APP_ORIGIN. Storefront links,
## the VNPay return URL and the public media base are derived from it.
## For production use backend/.env.prod.example instead.

APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost
# Dev pins the storefront dev server so email-verify/reset links work without
# the edge (nginx is stopped during `make dev-host`). Prod derives from
# APP_ORIGIN instead.
STOREFRONT_URL=http://localhost:3001

# See backend/.env.example for the full key reference.
# Local compose services / secrets for dev live in backend/.env.example too.

# Grafana Cloud Loki (log shipping via promtail). Create at grafana.com >
# Cloud (free tier) > stack > Connections > Loki; token scope: logs:write.
GRAFANA_LOKI_URL=
GRAFANA_LOKI_USER=
GRAFANA_LOKI_TOKEN=

# Grafana Cloud Tempo (trace shipping) — prod only. Dev leaves all of these
# unset: the dev compose default points OTel at the local jaeger:4318.
# Copy the OTLP endpoint + a traces:push token from the portal's
# \x22Send traces with OTLP\x22 page, then compute the Basic header:
#   powershell -Command \x22[Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes('USER:TOKEN'))\x22
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://otlp-gateway-prod-XX.grafana.net/otlp
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Basic <base64(instance-id:token)>
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.1
